Z||000000||MooCow||01-26-2001||12:55 PM||||HELP ME NOW!!!!!!!!!!!!!1<BR>I need help taking the darn door handle off.  How does it come off?????  It is making me mad and I need it off to take the body panels so I can paint it.  The part that goes from the handle down to the door catch I need off???????????????????????<P>                               Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kensig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||01-26-2001||04:10 PM||||If it's like most door handles, there is tool that slips behind the handle and around the crank shaft and will pop the retaining clip loose. Once the clip is out, the handle will come right off. Check with your local discount auto parts store. The tool will be less than $10.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||01-26-2001||05:41 PM||||Moo......!<P>LOL<BR>If your talking about the door handle on the outside of the car, here are the proper steps:<BR>1) Get chair<BR>2) Sit<BR>3) place both feet against door<BR>4) PULL REALLY REALLY HARD!<P>On a personal note, this method is not generally recommended!<P>The way that I do it is to remove the door skin to remove the nuts (2) that hold it on. Have fun!||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||01-26-2001||05:42 PM||||Take the inner door panel off. The linkage is held on by a little plastic clip. Hope you have small hands for reaching into there.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MooCow||01-26-2001||06:26 PM||||We got the handle off! No special tools neede.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   <P>                         Thanks Ken<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kensig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||7
